WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:07.040
Speaker 1: If we want to find some good&nbsp;
news in the data, it's that Democrats keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:14.240
gaining on Republicans in 2022 election&nbsp;
polling. The numbers are not yet a delight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:20.720
but they're increasingly looking. Okay. Let's&nbsp;
start with the house. Why start with the House?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:26.240
Well, Democrats are not favored to keep control of&nbsp;
the House. Democrats currently control the House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:32.000
of Representatives. It is likely that they will&nbsp;
lose the House of Representatives. But the numbers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:39.200
have been improving for Democrats every single day&nbsp;
for months. Where do the numbers stand now? The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:46.320
FiveThirtyEight forecast for the House says that&nbsp;
it's a 74% chance that Republicans take the House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:52.640
and a 26% chance that Democrats keep the House.&nbsp;
But look at the way the numbers have shifted.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:57.680
If you scroll down on this FiveThirtyEight&nbsp;
page, which is very, very detailed and it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:02.080
a great forecast, you will see a section&nbsp;
called How the House Forecast has Changed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:10.640
And you will see that in early June, Democrats&nbsp;
had a 14% chance of holding the House. That even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:21.600
dropped to 12 in late June, early July. But it has&nbsp;
been a steady but modest surge, almost doubling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:26.480
the odds of Democrats keeping the House going from&nbsp;
actually more than doubling, going from a bottom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:33.920
out of 12 to a 26% chance. Now, remember, things&nbsp;
that are 12% likely to happen sometimes happen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:40.560
things that are 26% likely to happen, sometimes&nbsp;
happen, but things that are 74% likely to happen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:46.480
are more likely to happen by definition. So I&nbsp;
can't tell you that I think it's a great shot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:52.400
for Democrats in the House, but the numbers have&nbsp;
been improving. And if Democrats keep adding on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:56.640
you know, a one percentage point chance&nbsp;
every other day between now and November,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:03.040
that's 30. Right. That would put this at 5050 by&nbsp;
Election Day. So that's what's happening in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:07.280
House. Now, in the Senate, things are looking&nbsp;
much better for Democrats. In the Senate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:14.880
Democrats are now 70%, 70% likely to hold control&nbsp;
of the Senate, whereas Republicans are only 30%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:20.240
likely. This has gone. Last week I told you it was&nbsp;
2 to 1 in favor of Democrats. It is now two and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:26.320
a third or whatever. It's well beyond 2 to 1 at&nbsp;
this point in time. And again, these are numbers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:31.680
that have improved for Democrats. There was a&nbsp;
point in early June where Democrats had a 40%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:38.960
shot of holding the Senate. That is now a 70%&nbsp;
shot. Very, very important to understand, because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:44.400
there are people writing to me saying, David, why&nbsp;
do you keep saying Democrats are going to have 70&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:51.680
senators? And of course, David is not saying that.&nbsp;
What I am telling you is that it is a 70% chance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.320 --> 00:03:00.000
that Democrats hold the Senate. The most&nbsp;
likely outcome is that Democrats hold it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:08.960
51 to 49. That would be a gain of one seat. Right&nbsp;
now in the Senate, it's 5050. The vice president&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:14.400
gets a tie breaking vote. That's Kamala&nbsp;
Harris. So Democrats are in the majority,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:22.800
5050 plus. Kamala, the most likely outcome&nbsp;
here is a 51 to 49 majority for Democrats. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:30.000
please do not write to me saying, David, Democrats&nbsp;
have no chance in hell of getting 70 seats. I'm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.920
agreeing with you. That's not what the number&nbsp;
means. That's not what the number means. But I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:41.920
appreciate everybody writing in. So the bottom&nbsp;
line, Democrats chances continuing to improve.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:47.520
And if they merely continue improving&nbsp;
at the same rate, the House will end up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:54.160
a 5050 flip of the coin by early November.&nbsp;
We will watch and see whether that happens.

